abstract: >-
  An evidence-driven Quality Engineering framework for testing hallucinations in
  Generative AI systems. The work defines a
  Claim-Evidence-Classify-Localize-Control-Gate model spanning unsupported and
  contradicted claims, fabricated entities, sources and actions, numerical and
  temporal errors, answerability, abstention, confidence language, deterministic
  validation, calibrated semantic judges, claim-level metrics, severity,
  hallucination root-cause localization, RAG and agentic failure modes,
  production-to-regression learning, baseline comparison, repeated-run
  stability, observability, missing-evidence handling and CI/CD release gates.
